WORKOS_API_KEY=sk_...
WORKOS_CLIENT_ID=client_...
WORKOS_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/auth/workos/callback
WORKOS_COOKIE_PASSWORD=replace-with-openssl-rand-base64-32-output
AUTH_WORKOS_LISTEN_ADDR=127.0.0.1:3000

# Google + Apple are AuthKit dashboard toggles, not process env.
# This package never reads GOOGLE_* or APPLE_* secrets. Do not add a second OAuth stack.
#
# Staging (WorkOS default credentials, no custom OAuth apps):
#   Dashboard → Authentication → OAuth providers
#   Google: Enable. Leave WorkOS default Client ID / Secret until production.
#   Sign in with Apple: Enable. Leave WorkOS default Team ID / Service ID / key until production.
# Email + password stays on; AuthKit enables it by default.
#
# Production (paste into the same dashboard dialogs, not into this file):
#   Google: your Google Client ID and Client Secret
#   Apple: Apple Team ID, Apple Service ID, Private Key ID, and the private key file
# See https://workos.com/docs/integrations/google-oauth
# and https://workos.com/docs/integrations/apple
